Mark XVII: update checker (signed manifest, report-only)

- updates.py: fetches a signed update manifest through the SSRF-guarded
  fetcher (size-capped, timeout added to guarded_fetch_bytes with the old
  default preserved), verifies its Ed25519 signature with the same public
  key that validates PRO licenses, and reports a newer release with notes
  and the download URL. Nothing is ever downloaded or installed
  automatically. Every failure mode returns a reason - offline-safe, no
  crash, no hang (4s timeout).
- Signature scheme: Ed25519 over the canonical JSON serialization of the
  manifest payload (sort_keys + tight separators); formatting differences
  on the wire cannot confuse verification. PRO-channel releases and the
  pro_url asset are surfaced only to PRO tiers.
- jarvis update check prints the result; a quiet background check runs on
  chat startup (daemon thread, opt-out via
  jarvis settings set updates.check_on_start=false).
- config: additive UpdatesConfig section (check_on_start, manifest_url) -
  schema stays v4, older configs load with defaults.
- Tests: signature verification (valid, tampered payload, tampered
  signature, malformed), version comparison (numeric-aware, v-prefix),
  offline fetch failure, mocked manifest round-trip, LITE pro_url hiding,
  non-JSON refusal. No network in tests (fetch is monkeypatched).
- Version 3.4.0.
